      "POCAHONTAS: I hear the wind.\nGRANDMOTHER WILLOW: Yes. What is it telling you?\nPOCAHONTAS: I don’t understand.",
      "GRANDMOTHER WILLOW: What do you see?\nPOCAHONTAS: Clouds!\nPOCAHONTAS: . Strange clouds.",
      "POCAHONTAS: We‘ll be all right.\nNAKOMA: We‘re gathering food for when the warriors arrive.",
      "NAKOMA: All right, what is it?\nPOCAHONTAS: What?\nNAKOMA: I know that look. You’re hiding something --\nPOCAHONTAS: I‘m not hiding anything. NAKOMA | Pocahontas, you can tell me. I promise I won‘t tell anyone...",
      "POCAHONTAS: Look again.\nGRANDMOTHER WILLOW: LET IT BREAK UPON YOU LIKE A WAVE UPON THE SAND"
    ]
